{
  "description": "Every popup, menu, picker's list and dialog the phone opens, opened on the parity rig's fixtures (Parity.kt) and drawn with every window composited where it sits (Measure.kt): out/popups/<theme>/<name>.png, and with the light one out/popups/<name>.json, each window's laid-out nodes. tests/parity/popups.py measures those and lays them out. `as` is the scenes.json scene (or a code-drawn one: custom) drawn first; `steps` are then done in order: tap, hold (a long-press), desc (tap by its description), type, flush, frame, lay, holdImage (a long-press on the first picture), code (a fixture: groups, find, ref, lookup, fixesWrite, meshModels, metaOpus) and toEnd. `measure`: `pane` names a text in an in-page pane (what's measured is the fill round it; `wide`: the page's width), `full` measures the screen's bar. `where` is how a user opens it; `kind` what it is.",
  "scenes": [
    {"name": "pop-home-main-menu", "what": "Home's ⋮ (Menu)", "where": "Home bar ⋮ (Menu)", "kind": "menu", "as": "home", "steps": [["tap", "Menu"]]},
    {"name": "pop-home-host-picker", "what": "Home's host picker (two hosts up)", "where": "Home, tap the host name beside New session (2+ hosts)", "kind": "dropdown", "as": "home", "steps": [["desc", "The host a new session"]], "threads": "bot-threads.json"},
    {"name": "pop-home-host-menu", "what": "Home's host picker, long-pressed", "where": "Home, long-press the host name", "kind": "menu", "as": "home-host-menu"},
